{
  "id": "ss.relic.ward",
  "name": "Warding scent",
  "description": "A charm of dried stems hung at a list — six of them, tawny and bile-green, cut ragged at the foot, lashed together with a crossed cord and a knot whose two ends hang loose, the tops splayed above the binding and two of them crossing, with a solid seed head still on three. A speck of arcane light comes in at the upper right and is bent away from the bundle in a short curve: the relic turns the next curse aside, and the deflection is the only thing here that says so. It is bound over most of its length and the fan is short, which keeps it a hung bundle and not a broom; the tilt and the crossed stems are there because an upright fan of five stems silhouetted as a raised hand, and the seed heads are solid because a pale head with a dark seed in it read as a loop with a hole.",
